Quick Recap

Basic → find(), find(condition)

Comparison → $gt, $lt, $gte, $lte, $eq, $ne

Logical → $or, $and, $not

Array match → $in, $nin

Regex → /^pattern/

Sort, limit, skip → organize results

1️⃣ Get All Documents
db.users.find()

2️⃣ Find with Condition
db.users.find({ city: "Bangalore" })

3️⃣ Show Only Certain Fields
db.users.find({ age: 22 }, { name: 1, city: 1 })
✅ Shows only name and city fields for age = 22.

4️⃣Comparison Queries

$eq → equal

$ne → not equal

$gt → greater than

$lt → less than

$gte → greater than or equal

$lte → less than or equal

👉 Example:

db.users.find({ age: { $gt: 20 } })      // age > 20
db.users.find({ age: { $lt: 30 } })      // age < 30
db.users.find({ age: { $gte: 18 } })     // age >= 18
db.users.find({ age: { $ne: 22 } })      // age != 22


5️⃣Logical Queries

$or → either condition

$and → both conditions

$not → opposite condition

$nor → none of the conditions

👉 Example:

db.users.find({
  $or: [ { city: "Bangalore" }, { age: { $lt: 23 } } ]
})

6️⃣ IN & NOT IN
db.users.find({ city: { $in: ["Bangalore", "Chennai"] } })
db.users.find({ city: { $nin: ["Delhi", "Mumbai"] } })


7️⃣ Pattern Matching (Regex)
db.users.find({ name: /^V/ })
✅ Finds users whose name starts with "V".

8️⃣ Sorting
db.users.find().sort({ age: 1 })   // ascending
db.users.find().sort({ age: -1 })  // descending

9️⃣ Limiting & Skipping
db.users.find().limit(2)    // first 2 results
db.users.find().skip(2)     // skip first 2 results
